<title>USA: Merrill Corp buys Superstar Computing.</title>
<headline>Merrill Corp buys Superstar Computing.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Corp on Monday said it acquired Superstar Computing, a provider of technology and software training services to the real estate industry, for an undisclosed price.</p>
<p>The company said Superstar Computing would operate as one of its subsidiaries and its founders and president would remain active in the business, Merrill said.</p>
<p>Merrill provides typesetting, printing and training services to the financial, legal, commercial and real estate industries.</p>
<p>Its shares were up 1-1/4 at 26-3/8 in late afternoon trading.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
